{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "type": "flow",
  "title": "How graph mode builds the @graph block",
  "description": "While the page renders, every schema component validates its props and registers its schema in a store kept per request and page in Astro.locals; <SchemaGraph /> renders only a placeholder. Once the page has fully rendered, the middleware resolves the page identity: the url of WebPageSchema, otherwise the site URL plus the page path. An article's mainEntityOfPage is pointed to that @id. If the page renders <SchemaGraph /> not exactly once, the build fails. Otherwise the placeholder is replaced by one script of type application/ld+json holding all schemas in an @graph array. With generateMeta, the canonical, Open Graph and Twitter tags of the primary schema, such as an article, are inserted into <head> as well, with the page @id as canonical URL.",
  "source": "src/components/Schema.astro, src/components/SchemaGraph.astro, src/middleware.ts, src/utils/graph.ts, src/utils/meta.ts, src/utils/json-ld.ts",
  "width": 1084,
  "height": 884,
